itadoriuji is a  fantastic character not because he's the  vessel for sukuna the king of curses  but because of how human he is despite  his superhuman strength  enhanced reflexes and his innate ability  to contain one of the biggest threats to  humanity  he has one defining characteristic that  is often overlooked  his selfish selflessness while in many  ways itadore yuji appears to be your  typical shonen protagonist  there is a reason why the story  surrounding him has gotten as popular  and enjoyable as it has  and that's because itadori is one of the  most relatable characters i've ever come  across  he's charming friendly and easy going  but he's also one of the loneliest  on the surface itadori is your typical  shonen protagonist high school student  as many quote-unquote straightforward  protagonists he gets portrayed as kind  adventurous and  somewhat simple academically speaking  however in his case this is a little bit  less extreme as with some of the more  idealistic characters such as luffy  naruto asta while these characters  represent certain ideals  expressed on a grander scale that the  audience can then look up to  i think itadori embodies a much more  down-to-earth and genuine version of  these traits with his one and only goal  being to live by the last words of his  grandfather  and that makes him less of an  unattainable ideal  and more of a relatable equal a big  portion of itadore's charm comes from  him being overall just a regular guy who  seems pretty fun to spend an afternoon  with this  also makes him a much more flexible and  malleable character with the ability to  look past animosity  and make friends of enemies we can see  this in his relationship with jumpe  and again later with his instant besto  friendo  todo and yet akutami the author of  jujutsu kaisen  doesn't shove it into our face that yuji  is a nice person  by having him deliver major speeches or  having other characters talk about what  a great guy he actually is  instead he leaves it for us to decide  what we think of him  in my mind he's pretty likable and  extroverted but  not overly so and at times there is a  certain awkwardness in his interactions  with his peers  his strong points are of course his  superhuman strength and his attitude for  jujutsu  but i think the actual power of his  comes from his extreme  altruism and his ability to act on  behalf of others  and yet as any good protagonist despite  itadore being an  awesome guy all around he still of  course  also has his weaknesses one thing that  isn't quite obvious from the start i  think  is that itadori actually has a really  strong sense of emptiness and loneliness  now since we know very little about his  past it's actually quite hard to tell  why this is the case despite his very  charismatic and extroverted nature  there is an answer to this question  however i believe the  fundamental flaw in itadore's  personality is actually the very same as  his strength  his altruism itadore yuji just like  luffy and the others  is an absolute genius when it comes to  people he's  extremely good at understanding them  what they're about  what drives them and how to handle them  but while he's  excellent at reading others he's  terrible at understanding himself  when we first meet itadori he has no  path  no drive and no meaningful relationships  in his life  except for his grumpy grandpa at school  even though he's absolutely notorious  for his physique he  doesn't have any real friends yes he  calls the two members of the occultist  club his friends but  they literally know nothing about him  also itadori only entered the club so he  could leave school early and visit his  grandpa in the first place  and so when he ultimately loses his  grandfather the  only person he was ever close to he  falls into grief and a very deep  sense of loneliness with no friends and  no purpose and suddenly presented with  the world of jiu-jitsu  itadori latches onto his grandfather's  dying wish  help others and die surrounded by  friends  and he's actually fully aware that this  is probably not the right thing to do  as he calls it his own curse  [Music]  [Music]  but with nothing else to hold on to it  thus  becomes his drive as a result we see  tadouri risking his life on a regular  basis  sometimes quite unnecessarily more than  once he just  rushes into situations with no regard  for his own health or life  and even though he admits that he's  scared of death he seems  way too eager to sacrifice himself for  others and thus try and give his life  meaning and purpose  this in my opinion quite toxic mindset  can be summarized like this  i must save and help others but i can't  receive help from anyone else  i must do everything myself this mindset  by the way  is also shared by itadore's counterpart  ghetto and so while itadore's altruism  is very much  real it is so extreme that ironically  enough  it starts to become selfish he wants to  do anything and  everything for others so that in return  he gets the validation and the  permission  to live his life the problem is when you  build relationships based on this  premise they  inevitably fall apart sooner or later  just as itadoris do  relationships are built on mutual  respect trust and sacrifice  and the buzzword here being mutual in  fulfilling his grandfather's wish and  his ultimate goal  itadori acts on his own and i think that  in searching for his purpose and wanting  to be needed  yuji enters the lives of other people  probably unconsciously  assuming that he can save them for  instance he does so for fushigoro and  jinpe but  very much disliked it himself when toto  does the very same thing to him at first  in short itadori looks for purpose and  validation  by making everything in his life about  others  therefore his character arc is all about  learning to form  real relationships built on mutual  feelings  mutual hardship mutual forgiveness and  mutual  sacrifice i think itadori's character  needs to find a real purpose  not to die for others but one that's  actually worth staying alive for  forming bonds that give meaning to his  life and make him appreciate  how precious it actually is the central  theme and moral argument of jiu-jitsu  kaisen is the question  what constitutes a good life that is  worth living andy tadouri as the main  protagonist  is starting his arc with a very  dangerous and self-destructive answer to  this question  [Music]  and yet the skill with which akutami is  able to expertly portray this weakness  as an underlying part of itadore's  personality  and only revealing it in tiny bits shows  his real skills as a writer  and makes itadori immediately immensely  relatable as a character  thus itadoriyuji is an extremely human  and realistic take on the comment shown  in tropes  that actually come very close to  togashi's way of writing however i  personally think that itadori's arc will  most likely come closer to that of kilua  from darkness into light  rather than guns fall into darkness and  i would even go as far as to say that  akutami's characters are even a tad more  complex and realistic in their design  satorugojo itadori's mentor comes to  mind here as well who is  eccentric intimidating funny and  so much more at the same time  these deep personalities complex  motivations and relationships  all combined with the gory and  fantasy-like elements set in a real  world setting have created a fantastic  story world for us to explore  and speaking of gojo you can watch his  analysis  right here thanks so much for watching  peace
 

